# C03 original action reader — send stopped, session attach closed

Issue: https://github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-remote-ops/issues/5
Repo: github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-ios
Branch: cursor/c03-original-action-reader-e504
Base: cursor/c03-route-page-readback-e504 @ db49be679c1f88cd334bd56ee17c7bd5a78d6bdf

`RouteActionReadbackFlow.swift` and `App/PlayRouteMapView.swift` are not rewritten.
The existing page already calls `RouteActionPageRead.shownRow`. This branch adds
`OriginalActionReader` and passes it in as that `selectAction`.

The reader asks `topicRouteSessionMapper.selectActionByAction` once. The row is
shown only when the session id, member id, and action id match. An absent id on
the row keeps the existing check. Appearance does not ask and does not write.
This branch does not insert a route action and does not rebuild the mapper.

## Real path

Looked up on hengyin, not copied into this repo:

- `master` `892efe6f765a5748065569fd886ee9b00ef71d4b`
- `cursor/c03-rpg-mechanism-consumers-5266` `eea786c064d3c1678c0dff621c9f56f9980ffa68`
- Method: `TopicRouteSessionMapper.selectActionByAction(sessionId, memberId, actionId)`
- XML: `TopicRouteSessionMapper.xml` `<select id="selectActionByAction">` on
  `topic_route_action` where `session_id`, `member_id`, and `action_id`, `limit 1`

No controller method calls that mapper. `GET /api/play/route-state` calls
`TopicRouteRuntimeServiceImpl.state` and does not call `selectActionByAction`.
POST action routes that replay through the mapper are writers. Neither is this query.

No HTTP path was found. This reader does not invent a path. `httpPath` stays nil.
`sends` stays 0. The send is stopped.

